{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541929-thaumaturgical-countermagic-against-mystical-discipline","id":1541929,"title":"Thaumaturgical Countermagic against \"Mystical\" Discipline","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-09-11T10:43:33-07:00","id":1541929,"title":"Thaumaturgical Countermagic against \"Mystical\" Discipline","content":"It is written that Thaumaturgical Countermagic is fully effective against Thaumaturgy only and halved against Necromancy and &quot;Mystical&quot; Disciplines.<br /> <br /> As it been stated before wich Discipline or Discipline's power are affected?<br /> I assume Potence, Celerity and Fortitude are not mystical since they're supernatural body enhancement as are many power from Protean and Vicissitude but what about Obneteration, Animalism, obfuscate and maybe above all Domination and Presence?<br /> <br /> Is it entirely on the St to draw the line?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-11T10:57:56-07:00","id":1541930,"title":"","content":"&quot;Mystical Disciplines&quot; is code for stuff we may or not include in the future that follows the same mechanics layout as Thaumaturgy but has a different name. Also, if you are playing in a cross over game, this is the mechanic you use to deal with hedge magic or the occasional use of true magic.<br /> <br /> The ST draws this line based on how much they want a vampire mage to be able to counter things like werewolf charms &amp; rituals, mage related shenanigans, or whatever obscure splat nonsense they are bringing in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-11T16:22:20-07:00","id":1541937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541929-thaumaturgical-countermagic-against-mystical-discipline?p=1541930#post1541930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The ST draws this line based on how much they want a vampire mage to be able to counter things like werewolf charms &amp; rituals, mage related shenanigans, or whatever obscure splat nonsense they are bringing in.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought Thaumaturgical countermagic was completely uneffective against non vampiric power, as written p.220 of V20, so it was logically referring to power from other Discipline. Or is there a mistake somewhere?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-11T16:45:46-07:00","id":1541938,"title":"","content":"Potency, Celerity and Fortitude are as mystical in this sense as anything else. There's no text saying they're enhancing the body in any particular way.<br /> <br /> That said, yes, it is entirely on the ST to draw the line. At the basic level it works against vampiric sorcery, that much is guaranteed, but from there it is a dial for the ST to select how they want Countermagic to affect the game.<br /> <br /> M20 too has explicit optional rules for the ST to decide how much True Magic is affected, with the default being that Thaumaturgical Countermagic works as normal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-12T06:42:04-07:00","id":1541971,"title":"","content":"Great, more work for me then x)<br /> How do you guys manage this against other Discipline? Is there a particular criterion you're using?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-12T10:22:18-07:00","id":1541978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541929-thaumaturgical-countermagic-against-mystical-discipline?p=1541937#post1541937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought Thaumaturgical countermagic was completely uneffective against non vampiric power, as written p.220 of V20, so it was logically referring to power from other Discipline. Or is there a mistake somewhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 220 in V20 covers &quot;Movement of the Mind&quot; and &quot;Path of Conjuring&quot; not counter magic.<br /> <br /> As for Thaumaturgical Countermagic on page 228, yes it does state that it is completely ineffective against non-vampire magics related magics, but to be fair this is one of the more consistent ST adjustments used to counter balance things like Mage &quot;I win&quot; buttons such as creating sunlight or just turning the vampire back into a normal human.<br /> <br /> This gets particularly messy when dealing with the Kuei-Jin and their rituals and magics because they are running off of Chi, but they are also vampires. So yeah, the ST gets to make judgement calls for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-12T14:38:31-07:00","id":1541993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541929-thaumaturgical-countermagic-against-mystical-discipline?p=1541971#post1541971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great, more work for me then x)<br /> How do you guys manage this against other Discipline? Is there a particular criterion you're using?</div> </div> </div> </div>Let it work for any power that's particularly versatile. Besides Vampiric Sorceries... Yeah, vampiric sorcery. If it works through Paths and Rituals, Countermagic counters. Other than that, add anything that's bothering you and you're having trouble countering.<br /> <br /> I'd say it works against True Magic, Changeling Arts and Demon Rituals. Garou usually have lots of options, but individually their powers are overly specific, so they're far less of a problem. Demon Lores, too. Its also thematically fitting that usual Countermagic don't work with them, or with spirits. Mummy and Wraith, I don't know, Hunters shouldn't ever be bothered by Countermagic.<br /> <br /> But seriously, the rule of thumb is if something is getting out of hand. Sorcery is countered because it is a cheap path to have a lot of distinct powers. If anything seems to be that kind of problem in your game, either a WIN button or a solution to everything, then check it with Countermagic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-13T13:54:20-07:00","id":1542072,"title":"","content":"Knowing that it's Thaumaturgical Countermagic, it's internally consistent to me for it to be an Art developed by Clan &amp; House Tremere with the Order of Hermes in mind. Developed during the First Massasa War, for use against the Clan's former allies among the Houses of Hermes. Possibly derived from House Tremere's old Countermagic principles from when they were Mages, adapted to function with Blood Sorcery.<br /> <br /> So, at least for me, I'm not against it working against True Magick. Definitely at full strength against other Hermetic arts (because they're directly matching like-to-like from a theory standpoint), and maybe half strength against non-Hermetic Magick. Barring ST fiat, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}